{#
The field classes, defined once.

The form theme (_layout/form/modal_form_theme.html.twig) styles every field a
Symfony form renders, and most of Settings is Symfony forms. The encryption
cards are not: they are drawn and driven by settings--encryption, or are plain
forms in the contacts' keys frame, so they hand-wrote their inputs — and the
hand-written copy had lost the theme's shadow, its disabled state and its
height, and its labels were a smaller, fainter size than every other label
in Settings. That was reported as "the textareas and inputs of the encryption
cards are unstyled" (#28, comment 6216080577).

So both draw from here: the theme's widget blocks and every hand-written field
return these strings, the way settings cards and admin panels share
_partials/_card_chrome.html.twig. Class strings and nothing else, for the
reason given there: the tokens (`bg-field`, `border-field`, `ring-accent`)
carry the theme's alpha and dark-mode variables, and a CSS @utility
re-deriving them would be the next copy to drift.

Usage:
    {% import '_partials/_field_classes.html.twig' as fields %}
    <label for="x" class="{{ fields.label() }} mb-2">…</label>
    <input id="x" class="{{ fields.input() }}">

A file input needs nothing from here beyond its width: its button is styled
for every file input there is, in app.css (`::file-selector-button`).
tests/e2e/settings-fields.spec.ts compares the encryption fields with a form
field of the theme, in both themes.
#}

{# A one-line field: text, email, password, search. #}
{% macro input() %}block w-full h-9 rounded-lg border border-field bg-field px-3 text-sm text-ink placeholder:text-ink-faint shadow-sm shadow-zinc-950/5 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent focus:border-transparent transition-colors duration-100 disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed{% endmacro %}

{# The same field over several lines; it grows downwards only. #}
{% macro textarea() %}block w-full rounded-lg border border-field bg-field px-3 py-2 text-sm text-ink placeholder:text-ink-faint shadow-sm shadow-zinc-950/5 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent focus:border-transparent resize-y transition-colors duration-100 disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed{% endmacro %}

{# A file input: full width, and the theme's disabled state. #}
{% macro file() %}block w-full text-xs disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed{% endmacro %}

{# A checkbox, as the theme's checkbox_widget draws it. `shrink-0` because a
   checkbox usually sits in a flex label beside a sentence, and a flex item
   gives way to the sentence: it rendered 13px wide beside the decrypted-mail
   consent instead of 16. #}
{% macro checkbox() %}size-4 shrink-0 rounded border-field accent-accent bg-field focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent focus:ring-offset-0 cursor-pointer{% endmacro %}

{# A field's label. The theme puts its gap in the row (`gap-2`); a hand-written
   field adds `mb-2` at the call site. #}
{% macro label() %}block text-[13px] font-medium leading-none text-ink-soft{% endmacro %}
